notes: "This is the feature I consider most important. History is kept per page, not for the whole deck. Open the History view, or right-click a slide in the Pages panel and choose View version history. Here is the 1BNA slide. Saved versions are named milestones: Before Matplotlib figure and Matplotlib figure were recorded around the change you just saw, and below them the earlier axis-label fix. Versions recorded from the command line are labelled human in this list, even though the agent recorded them. Operation history lists every saved change to that page, each with its review. And restoring a version changes only that slide; every other slide, and every talk that uses them, stays as it is. This is what replaces the folder of copies from the beginning of the talk."
